---
title: FAQ
description: Short answers to the questions players ask most about GGE Command, from bans and rubies to phones, languages and deleting your data.
---

Got a question? Here are the ones players ask most, with short answers and links to the details.

{% terms_on_page /%}

## Is GGE Command safe to use? {% #is-it-safe %}

Your game password is stored encrypted. Nobody can read it back, admins included, and GGE Command uses it only to sign in to the game for you.

The real risk is the game itself. Using a bot is against the game's rules, so read the next answer too.

## Can my game account get banned? {% #banned %}

Yes. Goodgame Empire can ban any {% term id="game-account" %}game account{% /term %} that uses a bot, and you take that risk. If a ban happens, the bot stops at once and you get a notification. Read [playing it safe](/playing-it-safe/) before you start, and see [what to do after a ban](/troubleshooting/#banned).

## Does the bot keep playing when my computer is off? {% #computer-off %}

Yes. Your bot works on GGE Command's own machines, not on your computer. Start it once, then close the browser or turn your computer off. It keeps playing until you stop it, its shutoff timer ends it, or something goes wrong. A schedule makes it sleep between the windows you set. See [how your bot runs](/how-your-bot-runs/).

## How many bots can I run? {% #how-many-bots %}

One for now. Each account can also have an event twin for a temporary event {% term id="server" %}server{% /term %}, and twins do not count. See [add a game account](/war-room/dashboard/#add-account).

{% plan_gate %}
Your plan decides how many bots you can run. See [plans](/plans/).
{% /plan_gate %}

## Which servers can I play on? {% #servers %}

Any server in the list when you add an account. The list comes from the game's own list of worlds, and GGE Command keeps it up to date. Pick the server you play on, or the bot can't sign in. If yours is missing, see [SERVER_UNKNOWN](/errors/#server-unknown).

## Which languages does the app speak? {% #languages %}

The app speaks 28 languages. With {% ui key="common:language.automatic" /%}, it picks one from your country and your browser. You can [change the language](/war-room/settings/#language) at any time.

## Does the bot spend my rubies? {% #rubies %}

Most modules never spend rubies. Two modules can, and only after you change their settings:

- [Auto Station](/modules/alert-autostation/) can open your gates for rubies when no alliance castle takes your troops. This is **Off** until you turn it on, and you set the most one opening may cost.
- [Invasion events](/modules/invasion-events/) rent a harder difficulty for rubies only if you pick one by hand. Dethroning a camp with Fortify costs rubies, and it stays off until you set its limits above 0.

[Storms](/modules/storms/) can buy time skips, but it pays with aquamarine, not rubies, and this is off by default. The [wheel spin](/modules/wheel-spin/) never buys a jackpot. [Recruit, tools and heal](/modules/recruit-tools-heal/) pays only with coins and resources.

## Can I use GGE Command on my phone? {% #phone %}

Yes. The app works in your phone's browser, and its pages fit a small screen. The bot plays the browser game Goodgame Empire only for now. It does not play the mobile game Empire: Four Kingdoms.

## How do I stop all my bots at once? {% #stop-everything %}

On the [Overview page](/war-room/dashboard/#start-stop), tick the box in the header of the roster. It ticks every account on the page. Then choose {% ui key="common:action.stop" /%}. A stopped bot stays stopped until you start it again.

## Can I choose when the bot plays? {% #schedule %}

Yes. Open the account, choose the {% ui key="client:drawer.schedule" /%} tab and turn on {% ui key="client:schedule.toggle" /%}. The bot then works only inside the windows you set and sleeps in between. See [the bot is sleeping](/troubleshooting/#sleeping).

## Why does a number on the Overview page have a plus? {% #plus-sign %}

Attacks and errors are counted from the {% term id="log" %}log{% /term %} lines kept for each account: the newest 500, and none older than 7 days. A plus means some lines may have been dropped, so the real number is at least that. See [the figures at the top](/war-room/dashboard/#figures).

## What does "Game said not now" mean? {% #not-now %}

The game refused something for now, such as during a cooldown or with a full queue. It passes by itself, and the bot tries again later. These lines are not errors. See [the four levels](/war-room/logs/#levels).

## How do I delete my data? {% #delete-data %}

To remove one game account, tick it on the Overview page and choose {% ui key="common:action.remove" /%}. To delete everything, open [Settings](/war-room/settings/#delete-account) and choose {% ui key="client:delete.button" /%}. Choose {% ui key="client:export.button" /%} first if you want a copy.

## Is GGE Command made by Goodgame Studios? {% #goodgame %}

No. GGE Command is not affiliated with Goodgame Studios. See the [disclaimer](/disclaimer/).
